  "summary": "Liberty (MO) police used the Flock ALPR database to locate a missing man with Alzheimer's who had driven away from home; a Clay County Sheriff's deputy responded to a camera ping and returned him safely. The article is paired with a 'Heart of the Matter' segment featuring privacy concerns about license plate readers.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "A Liberty Police Department officer entered the vehicle's license plate number into the Flock database to try to find him.",
      "paragraph_idx": 4
    },
    {
      "quote": "A Clay County Sheriff's Office deputy heard that one of the Flock cameras pinged the man's license plate about an hour and a half later.",
      "paragraph_idx": 5
    },
    {
      "quote": "A combination of technology and caring led to the man getting home safely",
      "paragraph_idx": 7
    }
  ],
